<title>DUBAI: UAE signs airport deal with Siemens Plessey System.</title>
<headline>UAE signs airport deal with Siemens Plessey System.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates on Wednesday awarded a 44 million dirham air traffic control system deal to British company Siemens Plessey Systems, the official news agency WAM said,</p>
<p>Under the agreement, the firm, a unit of Germany's Siemens AG, will deliver a state-of-the-art system for Abu Dhabi airport -- the last part of a major modernisation plan at UAE airports, it added.</p>
<p>Transport Ministry secretary-general Matar Humaid al-Tayer signed the deal with a company official. WAM gave no further details.</p>
</text>
